  "prefLabel": "Rko 214.07 Review of Requests for Rehearing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rko 214.07 Review of Requests for Rehearing. If a request for rehearing is filed within 30 days of the date of the presiding officer’s decision, the ombudsman shall, within 10 days of the receipt of the request, grant a rehearing, if it appears from the record that:\n\na. The decision was unlawful or unreasonable; and\n\nb. Receipt of additional evidence, argument, or analysis is necessary to reach a decision that is lawful and reasonable.",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rko100-200.html"
